{
  "$comment": [
    "Fontstacks published to tiles.openwaters.io/fonts. A stack is one MapLibre `text-font`",
    "entry; the `sources` list is merged into it, so worldwide coverage is a font list rather",
    "than a code problem. Names are the stack names a style asks for and must stay stable —",
    "changing one breaks every published style that references it.",
    "",
    "Weights stop at SemiBold and widths at normal, deliberately. Only the Latin face has",
    "italics — no Noto script family ships one — so an italic stack is Latin-italic over upright",
    "fallbacks, and the Condensed widths have no non-Latin counterpart at all, which would make a",
    "Condensed stack silently tofu outside Latin. Thin and ExtraLight are wrong for a chart on",
    "their own terms: hairline strokes disappear under glare, and S-4 B-412.4 reserves hairline",
    "numerals for soundings of LOWER RELIABILITY, so the weight would carry a meaning nobody",
    "intended. Scripts lacking a given weight fall back to their Regular rather than vanishing.",
    "",
    "Chart use: Italic is the sloping default for soundings (S-4 B-412.1); Regular is upright,",
    "which is also B-412.4's posture for low-reliability soundings; Medium and SemiBold buy",
    "legibility at smaller sizes, where a halo eats a light stroke."
  ],
